comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-19T09:03:37.249Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all-status PM corpus for CodSpeed cache instruments, Valgrind/libc6-dbg, benchmark workflow timeout, and cancellation. pm-yh6t is the completed adoption lineage and explicitly remains canonical for benchmark evidence, but no item tracks this repeated hosted setup regression; this issue is its focused regression child. GitHub evidence: PR #1062 exact-head run 32233697787/job 96008873672 restored the instrument cache, began installing /tmp/valgrind-codspeed.deb and libc6-dbg, never started Vitest, and was canceled at 20m20s."
  "2026-08-19T09:13:08.931Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: kept CodSpeed v5.0.3 in deterministic simulation mode and disabled only instrument caching. The two exact-head failures restored cached Valgrind artifacts before stalling; CodSpeed's documented v5 input permits cache-instruments=false, and its action key includes mode, OS, architecture, kernel, and runner version but not the GitHub hosted-image revision. Focused CI workflow contract passed 13/13; typecheck, ESLint, zero-clone jscpd, package/SDK/static gates, tracker-context-quality, and audit (zero known vulnerabilities) passed after replacing the initial generic edge with typed implementation lineage."
  "2026-08-19T09:17:49.276Z","harness:codex","Hosted acceptance: PR #1062 exact head a09dc7a4847b969bea1f88671d96aca7e5fa9408, CodSpeed run 32236517929/job 96017597363 completed successfully in 3m42s. The action reached all 11 BM25, pagination, and text-normalization benchmarks, emitted the benchmark summary, and uploaded performance data for unbraind/pm-cli. This replaces two prior 20m20s cancellations that never started Vitest."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-19T09:13:09.454Z","harness:codex",A third-party action cache can be less deterministic than a fresh install when its key fingerprints the kernel but not the hosted image revision; preserve the measurement instrument and disable the narrower stale cache rather than weakening the benchmark to walltime or extending a timeout around an install that never progresses.
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  .github/workflows/codspeed.yml,project,Disable stale CodSpeed instrument cache while retaining simulation mode
  tests/integration/ci-workflow-contract.spec.ts,project,Lock CodSpeed measurement mode and no-cache setup contract
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/integration/ci-workflow-contract.spec.ts,project,240
test_runs[1]{run_id,kind,status,started_at,finished_at,recorded_at,passed,failed,skipped}:
